Id: encoding-sub-options-honoured
Title: The options of the encoding repair are honoured by fix_text()
Input: Any text given to fix_text() with one of the options
 restore_byte_a0, replace_lossy_sequences, decode_inconsistent_utf8 or
 fix_c1_controls set to FALSE by name, where that option changes what
 the encoding repair does. For example 'voil\u00c3  le travail' (two
 spaces after the first word) with restore_byte_a0, '\u00c3\ufffdtude'
 with replace_lossy_sequences,
 '\u2603 caf\u00c3\u00a9' with decode_inconsistent_utf8 and
 '\u0094\u044f' with fix_c1_controls.
Reference: The option is not passed on to the encoding repair when it
 is given to fix_text() as a keyword argument, so the encoding is
 repaired as with default options. fix_text() then makes a config with
 explain=False (ftfy/__init__.py:341), and fix_and_explain() calls
 fix_encoding(text) with no config when it does not explain
 (ftfy/__init__.py:396). Run on ftfy 6.3.1 with Python 3.13:
 fix_text('voil\xc3  le travail', restore_byte_a0=False) returns
 'voil\xe0 le travail' (one space), fix_text('\xc3\ufffdtude',
 replace_lossy_sequences=False) returns '\ufffdtude',
 fix_text('\u2603 caf\xc3\xa9', decode_inconsistent_utf8=False) returns
 '\u2603 caf\xe9' and fix_text('\x94\u044f', fix_c1_controls=False)
 returns '"\u044f': each is what fix_text() returns with no option. The
 option is honoured when it comes in a config object, which explains
 unless told not to: fix_text('voil\xc3  le travail',
 TextFixerConfig(restore_byte_a0=False)) returns 'voil\xe0  le travail'
 (both spaces), and the other three return '\xc3\ufffdtude',
 '\u2603 caf\xc3\xa9' and '\x94\u044f'. fix_encoding() and
 fix_encoding_and_explain() honour the option in both forms. So does
 fix_and_explain() while it explains, which it does unless its config
 says explain=False: fix_and_explain('voil\xc3  le travail',
 TextFixerConfig(explain=False, restore_byte_a0=False)) returns the text
 'voil\xe0 le travail' (one space).
R: The option is honoured however it is given, by name or in a config
 made by ftfy_config(), and fix_text() gives what the reference version
 gives for the option in a TextFixerConfig: 'voil\xe0  le travail'
 (both spaces), '\xc3\ufffdtude', '\u2603 caf\xc3\xa9' and '\x94\u044f'
 for the four calls above. This package has no option explain and its
 other functions give what the reference version gives while it
 explains, so the difference is seen only in fix_text() with one of the
 four options given by name. With default options nothing differs.
Decided: docs/adr/0001-options-as-named-arguments-over-a-config-object.md
